WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.764
In this video, you will learn how to find holiday lights and events near you.

00:00:04.764 --> 00:00:11.142
We will cover the season buttons, searching by city, getting driving routes, and narrowing the list with filters.

00:00:11.142 --> 00:00:12.261
We start on the map.

00:00:13.164 --> 00:00:17.226
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:17.226 --> 00:00:19.351
That is the only address you need.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.799
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:23.799 --> 00:00:27.344
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:27.344 --> 00:00:28.673
Tap Use my location.

00:00:28.673 --> 00:00:33.168
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:34.978 --> 00:00:37.390
Your browser asks permission as well.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.089
Tap Allow.

00:00:38.089 --> 00:00:42.786
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:45.206 --> 00:00:46.986
The map zooms to where you are.

00:00:46.986 --> 00:00:51.158
There are no events on your street, so tap Show all of Southern California.

00:00:52.956 --> 00:00:57.713
Now every place shows how far away it is, nearest first, so you can plan your drive.

00:00:59.675 --> 00:01:04.663
The map shows different things at different times of the year, so first choose a season.

00:01:04.663 --> 00:01:06.569
Tap the season button at the top.

00:01:06.569 --> 00:01:08.251
It shows what is on right now.

00:01:10.304 --> 00:01:11.634
Pick the one you want.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:16.029
Christmas lights are the biggest, so tap Thanksgiving and Christmas Lights.

00:01:16.029 --> 00:01:19.499
Halloween, New Year, and other seasons are in the same list.

00:01:21.332 --> 00:01:23.222
You can also search for a city.

00:01:23.222 --> 00:01:25.525
Type its name, and tap it in the list.

00:01:25.525 --> 00:01:31.786
The map jumps there, which is handy if you are planning a trip to a different part of Southern California.

00:01:33.945 --> 00:01:37.316
To drive to what you see, tap Route these, under the list.

00:01:37.316 --> 00:01:40.516
It puts everything currently showing into driving order.

00:01:42.416 --> 00:01:48.828
Your maps app can only take about nine stops at a time, so a long list is split into routes of nine or fewer.

00:01:48.828 --> 00:01:53.608
Each route starts where the last one ended, so you do not have to plan the break.

00:01:53.608 --> 00:01:58.096
And you can tick off places as you go, so you can pick up where you left off.

00:01:59.793 --> 00:02:01.746
To narrow the list, tap Filters.

00:02:01.746 --> 00:02:10.444
You can pick a date, like tonight or this weekend, a distance from where you are, a type, such as free events, or walk through displays, and more.

00:02:10.444 --> 00:02:12.870
Use it when the list is too long to scan.

00:02:15.149 --> 00:02:17.493
That is how you find lights near you.

00:02:17.493 --> 00:02:20.886
Allow your location, so distances and directions work.

00:02:20.886 --> 00:02:21.811
Pick a season.

00:02:21.811 --> 00:02:22.736
Search a city.

00:02:22.736 --> 00:02:24.834
And narrow the list with Filters.

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:27.671
In the next video, we will plan a whole night.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.563
Next up: Plan a night.
